WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.360
Today we've actually unlocked the next step&nbsp;
along the Teign Estuary Trail. It's been a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:10.440
project that's long been wanted by people in&nbsp;
Teignmouth and Newton Abbot. It's about getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:17.720
a cycle way all the way from Teignmouth through to&nbsp;
Newton Abbot along the side of the Teign Estuary.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:22.120
For a long time it's been stuck we've got&nbsp;
Planning Permission but we don't have the money,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:26.600
we don't have the land, so we can't ask for&nbsp;
the money. What we've done today is opened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:31.760
up a way of actually getting that land and&nbsp;
building a business case so we'll create a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:36.600
right of access along the side of the Teign&nbsp;
Estuary and a business case so we can appeal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:42.360
to government to get the project completed. Today&nbsp;
we brought forward a million pounds of community&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:47.960
infrastructure Levy money paid by developers to&nbsp;
help us develop new things like cycle paths to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:53.000
actually make this project happen and this is&nbsp;
a fantastic collaboration between Teignbridge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:01.400
Devon County, the Teign Estuary Trail campaign&nbsp;
group and Bishopsteignton Parish Council,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:05.640
and together we're making a real difference for&nbsp;
local residents in the area. So the next steps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.640
now we've got the money allocated is to do the&nbsp;
work to build the business case to prove that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:15.880
it's going to be a good investment to purchase&nbsp;
the bits of land along the side of the river and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:19.560
then to make a right of way through that, so&nbsp;
at least we've got a footpath that will be an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:24.600
off-road footpath from Bishopsteignton through&nbsp;
to Passage House in Kingsteignton on the side&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:30.400
of the river on through into Newton Abbot. That&nbsp;
in itself will be extremely valuable when we've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.040
got that ready and we've got a business case we&nbsp;
can then appeal to the next round of government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:41.160
funding - whenever that may be - and say "here's&nbsp;
our project we're ready to go, give us the money."

